only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378247} {:answer/id #uuid "94d62c48-c41c-5fbc-9d7a-f4d1a6557b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378248} {:answer/id #uuid "56d6d423-5656-501e-b2f6-2c600eecf510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fddf6f5d-eb46-55d9-bafa-dfcde8802b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ce217c-40ee-5b1e-ac1e-80701505ad04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "097f179d-8b94-55d4-8f36-ac53f5125474" :question/math-academy-id "q-104930" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\n- $P(N)$\n- $P({Z,\\pi })$\n- $P({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})$" :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is infinite since the underlying set $N$ is infinite.\n\n- Set II is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,\\pi })={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{\\pi },\\,{Z,\\pi }}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0}={0},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})=P({0})={∅,\\,{0}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "495f3da0-849a-589d-ac88-26d6825445e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Subsets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058a0bec-443e-5691-ba0f-473fbc4a32ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253710} {:answer/id #uuid "136d7516-047a-5f19-b65a-d650137e6cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253838} {:answer/id #uuid "3212f762-64a0-547c-90de-3d647c6ae143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254102} {:answer/id #uuid "54d746d5-3697-5980-8711-62bace1a807a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254410} {:answer/id #uuid "666f6e15-03ca-5add-9346-421f3637c229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3212f762-64a0-547c-90de-3d647c6ae143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254102} :answer-field/id #uuid "1553d09e-038b-5d1a-b170-1ab51570b9d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0906e8f1-346b-507f-9289-d9fb6006311a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1210" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in Z:-2\\le x<6}$ and $B={x\\in N:x+1<6}?$\n\n- $∅⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊈B$" :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all integer numbers greater than or equal to $-2$ but less than $6.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $x+1<6.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2,3,4}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $∅⊆B$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $-1\\in A$ but $-1\\notin B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "196e093f-03be-5f08-b076-d621b0e1f3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257000} {:answer/id #uuid "53f30868-1437-5931-801c-542ae9db9646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257501} {:answer/id #uuid "c68f82ae-5663-5f1b-b44f-c2c9f755251a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258518} {:answer/id #uuid "f147f689-f111-564c-8b19-a90facfa2838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258881} {:answer/id #uuid "f6913a70-bd5e-5927-a8ff-79c39dc44ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f147f689-f111-564c-8b19-a90facfa2838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258881} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f7066f-d0c9-5b83-af5b-6f18771d4180" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c012134a-99e0-5f06-b534-c2d2ae072768" :question/math-academy-id "q-1257" :question/problem "For the sets $A={2,4,6},$ $B={x,y},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(2,4)\\in C$\n- $(2,x)\\in C$\n- $(3,y)\\in C$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/df/df4277feac4c4e838538f941aa0a07d087beb9005d8f7a8347dadc1da7fe975e.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(2,x),(2,y),(4,x),(4,y),(6,x),(6,y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae566481-20f8-5e52-99d8-23a6c82691b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051501} {:answer/id #uuid "cdadc5ef-7415-5dcf-b7cf-505d2e49c925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051502} {:answer/id #uuid "d138c6e0-6807-55b7-ab39-2b7416f93002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051503} {:answer/id #uuid "4129157c-b81d-59dd-8ec5-f67444db60ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051504} {:answer/id #uuid "574a525d-c730-52ff-a8ed-06f70442fbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051505}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd58087-ae96-5ce0-a2c8-bc32e79b782d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051500}] :question/id #uuid "1ff208f5-5023-5db1-8017-ca1f7ce1c080" :question/math-academy-id "q-1262" :question/problem "For the sets $Z = {-1, 0, 1}$ and $Y = Z \\cdot Z$, determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n1. $(-1, 0, 1) ∈ Y$\n2. $(-1, 1) ∈ Y$\n3. $(0, 0) ∈ Y$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b65e0d-e0ec-5c78-83e7-464d161c710e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282040} {:answer/id #uuid "981fa0bd-1eab-533b-a3bd-408d47bff141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283005} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd70cf2-89b7-5b7d-9e01-1bad692f732d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283337} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc0aa08-8957-55c6-a911-6a19c3aeab6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283487} {:answer/id #uuid "d42a75bf-c403-5ab9-a1a6-c356df5be84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28b65e0d-e0ec-5c78-83e7-464d161c710e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282040} :answer-field/id #uuid "749096d0-da42-556e-9777-a6ec85e594b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a13c06f-6317-5f54-a60c-2244cd05e4c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-170843" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:2\\,|\\,4$\n\n- $Q:\\sqrt{2}\\in N$\n\n- $R:2+2$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $2$ divides $4.$\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $\\sqrt{2}$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b977c97-5651-5521-8e42-8586c819737b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281942} {:answer/id #uuid "4837ea75-c829-536a-a4b9-0330dad23871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282300} {:answer/id #uuid "757a25c4-109e-5e2c-b7d3-4592990f5a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282695} {:answer/id #uuid "88befc2b-a69f-5e4c-8302-6401c5b5bd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282868} {:answer/id #uuid "d980bec9-678b-539f-9be7-a1eec6774c12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88befc2b-a69f-5e4c-8302-6401c5b5bd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282868} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2cb3a4-04dc-56b8-b5b9-48858253e5be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d26247f5-ea0b-58f7-ab8c-9e2873f56e29" :question/math-academy-id "q-170844" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:{1,2,3}\\cap {4,5,6}=∅$\n\n- $Q:\\sqrt{{3}^{2}-{4}^{2}}$\n\n- $R:4$ is a prime number." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because the intersection of the given sets is empty.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *false* since $4$ is not prime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b66c561-2d7c-52e3-937c-7c67a5e4c9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281795} {:answer/id #uuid "8f92b8fc-c666-5069-b9ed-7cca08c7478a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282933} {:answer/id #uuid "9168ac28-6e40-58c9-bed3-110b24af01c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282948} {:answer/id #uuid "ae15b0f1-3036-51bd-baa5-b49cc5514bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283194} {:answer/id #uuid "baeeb572-5d5f-5a04-9e96-fb8e01c8b8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae15b0f1-3036-51bd-baa5-b49cc5514bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283194} :answer-field/id #uuid "880dbba7-c9a6-57c2-abf2-7f956c2c632b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5327827-bdd3-59f2-8ac3-6f2fcb1af21e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171486" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\n- $P(n):$ $n$ is even.\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}-x\\ge 1$\n- $R(y):$ Draw a line of width $y\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give an instruction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2316f533-0e7d-5b77-a8dd-d9c80337923d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285102} {:answer/id #uuid "2c25e9a3-12f8-5ff9-b8bc-23630a88a7fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285174} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3b07df-dd5d-5565-a9c1-e98ca207f466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285623} {:answer/id #uuid "97d4e979-a44a-50ce-9b33-412cccd7bc2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286174} {:answer/id #uuid "d6189dc5-6bc6-5726-a93c-14409fffef6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b3b07df-dd5d-5565-a9c1-e98ca207f466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285623} :answer-field/id #uuid "864bb7c7-2e83-595f-ad2e-7f0fc29c9ab4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59457bab-d41c-5c4d-af91-59c9dc67dad9" :question/math-academy-id "q-181294" :question/problem "If $A={0,1,2}$ and $B={x,y},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A\\times B)\\times A?$\n\n- $(1,y,2)$\n- $((1,y),2)$\n- $((y,1),y)$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${0,1,2}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/07/077da578323a686ecf0e07cf0a56030fa4ce128a74d408af95b8a3027ad13f28.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(0,x),(0,y),(1,x),(1,y),(2,x),(2,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=3\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/3a/3a14abffc755dcfccce2d410ea18fbcae42d4afe2fbeffd81e1a291bc9d4968e.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A\\times B)\\times A|=|A\\times B|\\cdot |A|=6\\cdot 3=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $((1,y),2)\\in (A\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "159275ce-4dc9-57f1-827a-d1275c32d42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284979} {:answer/id #uuid "2ec53427-0975-56a7-a33f-29f2ec5b5a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285207} {:answer/id #uuid "377afc5a-c99c-58b1-869c-9949866416fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285308} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb6250f-9c76-5e92-a1ee-5eedcf4fdb74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285360} {:answer/id #uuid "9abd151c-b575-5dc9-a22a-1b6338ae760c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "377afc5a-c99c-58b1-869c-9949866416fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285308} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2f51709-2790-5816-b247-4202c39421bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eac2d72-9d93-50cd-8b4e-008064a9d365" :question/math-academy-id "q-181295" :question/problem "If $A={-1,1}$ and $B={u,v},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times B\\times A?$\n\n- $(v,v,1)$\n- $((v,v),1)$\n- $(1,v,u)$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${u,v}$ with ${u,v}$ and ${-1,1},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\times B\\times A={ & (u,u,-1),(u,u,1),(u,v,-1),(u,v,1), \\\\  & (v,u,-1),(v,u,1),(v,v,-1),(v,v,1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|B\\times B\\times A|=|B|\\cdot |B|\\cdot |A|=2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(v,v,1)\\in B\\times B\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fda93df-ceee-5bdb-bcc8-1d50dfc0498d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285074} {:answer/id #uuid "2c766e6e-b354-5cb5-9c36-def341ed3a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285177} {:answer/id #uuid "73dbea24-3b14-53be-ad68-7aabf8690471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N,Z,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285854} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf79b26-6875-5dda-b273-4bc2013c9321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286511} {:answer/id #uuid "d81191ac-5930-5912-8558-b840f6af73bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81191ac-5930-5912-8558-b840f6af73bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286754} :answer-field/id #uuid "05e9342c-22e5-53ad-8a49-1010cc6022ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d88d3c9d-ec93-5bf2-a49b-0b326607c0ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-181441" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\sqrt{-1}$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-1}=\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-1}$ is nonzero, it does not belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4e7efc6-2907-5146-bf87-e5dadaa7ef87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A, B$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052119} {:answer/id #uuid "113d6841-6789-509b-8adf-0487e9a14aed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052120} {:answer/id #uuid "25076717-a6b6-5e26-b5d4-9eeb494aa9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052121} {:answer/id #uuid "7172bb65-a488-55f3-85a5-2a897483409f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052122} {:answer/id #uuid "798a3ace-bf62-53c2-b076-4cb83ba3fcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052123}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d5226921-bc7e-5b2a-be0c-3dc1f726fdb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052118}] :question/id #uuid "591488e6-be15-5117-89a8-9b785af2738a" :question/math-academy-id "q-22405" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c63af2b4cd9209077baee74e5f4f4059bc1c8c7e4b2cdc620c872d025fe5a4e9.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y = x + 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0e5efaa-e624-5045-abdb-cdf8d32ad6cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subsets of a Given Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008b14e2-2eb7-5860-a87e-0160df06982a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321155} {:answer/id #uuid "37b51cee-e47f-5389-8754-e6cb41bb1d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321571} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2afd22-c826-5f07-b793-9425e286c5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321859} {:answer/id #uuid "a379458a-8455-599b-b6ee-19fe7a08b429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322435} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e64f5a-4b71-5bc7-981a-e174acbf1276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b51cee-e47f-5389-8754-e6cb41bb1d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321571} :answer-field/id #uuid "692fcb01-3089-5ea3-b724-d5b3f46f2b2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8e8eb5c8-f406-5cdf-99fb-6d6cbbcd6c06" :question/math-academy-id "q-37255" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={{1},{2,3},{1,3,6}}?$\n\n- ${2,{1}}$\n- ${{2,3}}$\n- ${{-1},{1,3,6}}$" :question/worked-solution "A set is a subset of $A$ if all its elements are elements of $A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each option.\n\n- ${2,{1}}$ is *not* a subset of $A$ because it contains the element $2\\notin A.\\,\\times $\n\n- ${{2,3}}$ is a subset of $A.\\,✓$\n\n- ${{-1},{1,3,6}}$ is *not* a subset of $A$ because it contains the element ${-1}\\notin A.\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b6fdc7-1ea3-5594-a5a6-9cae3b4ea745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321798} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5f6106-957d-5dab-b250-9423ea39f089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321996} {:answer/id #uuid "9537bac4-9f3d-5267-92a8-65878ddcc632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592